    "title": "TSA to Charge Fee for Non-REAL ID Flyers Starting February 1, 2026",
    "text": "• The Transportation Security Administration (TSA) announced a $45 fee for U.S. flyers without a REAL ID or approved alternative, starting February 1, 2026.\n• The fee can be paid online before arriving at the airport or at the airport before entering the security line.\n• The verification process could take 10 to 30 minutes.\n• Paying the fee does not guarantee verification.\n• If approved, the verification covers a 10-day travel period.\n• TSA says the fee will help pay for operational expenses and encourage people to obtain a REAL ID.\n• Acceptable forms of ID include passports, military IDs, permanent resident cards, and photo IDs from federally recognized tribal nations.\n• TSA accepts digital IDs through platforms like Apple Wallet, Google Wallet, and Samsung Wallet at over 250 U.S. airports.\n• The REAL ID requirement began in May, with travelers without it facing a longer screening process.",
